  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6562 added the `ImageDataSettings` interface as part of color space support for canvases--it's an options dict that's passed into the `ImageData` constructors and canvas' `ImageData` factory methods.\r\n\r\nThis breaks with the naming convention for all other options dictionaries, which are named `Options` and not `Settings` (e.g. [ImageEncodeOptions](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#imageencodeoptions), [ElementDefinitionOptions](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#elementdefinitionoptions), etc.)\r\n\r\nI'm not well-versed with the finer details of the spec but I don't believe the interface name is exposed anywhere in the API itself, so renaming `ImageDataSettings` to `ImageDataOptions` should be a completely normative change.",
